.TH std::move_iterator::base 3 "2026.11.10" "http://cppreference.com" "C++ Standard Libary"
.SH NAME
std::move_iterator::base \- std::move_iterator::base

.SH Synopsis
iterator_type base() const;                                    (constexpr since C++17)
                                                       \fB(1)\fP     \fI(until C++20)\fP
constexpr const iterator_type& base() const& noexcept;         \fI(since C++20)\fP
constexpr iterator_type base() &&;                         \fB(2)\fP \fI(since C++20)\fP

Returns the underlying iterator.

1) Returns a
copy of
\fI(until C++20)\fP
reference to
\fI(since C++20)\fP the underlying iterator.
2) Returns an iterator move constructed from the underlying iterator.

.SH Return value

1) current
2) std::move(current ﻿)

.SH Example


// Run this code

#include <algorithm>
#include <iostream>
#include <iterator>
#include <vector>

int main()
{
    std::vector<int> v{0, 1, 2, 3, 4};
    std::move_iterator<std::vector<int>::reverse_iterator>
        m1{v.rbegin()},
        m2{v.rend()};

    std::copy(m1.base(), m2.base(), std::ostream_iterator<int>(std::cout, " "));
    std::cout << '\\n';
}

.SH Output:

4 3 2 1 0

